  <!-- Section 6: Common Tech Pack Mistakes -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Common Tech Pack Mistakes That Delay Production</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        This section builds expert credibility by identifying specific tech pack mistakes that cause production delays and costly revisions. Most mistakes stem from incomplete specifications, vague descriptions, or missing critical information. Manufacturers must guess when specifications are unclear, and guessing inevitably leads to errors. The following eight mistakes are the most common causes of tech pack-related production delays. Avoid these to ensure smooth, accurate production.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Missing measurements is the most common mistake. Without complete measurement specs for each size, manufacturers guess dimensions based on standard grading rules, which may not match your intended fit. This leads to samples that don't fit correctly, requiring multiple rounds of fit samples and pattern revisions. Pantone numbers not specified is another frequent error - without Pantone numbers, manufacturers match colors visually, which results in inconsistent color across production runs. Fabric weight not stated leads to wrong hand feel and drape, as the same fabric in different weights behaves differently in production.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        No seam allowance noted causes manufacturers to add seam allowances differently than intended, affecting fit and construction. Missing construction notes for complex areas like collar stands, plackets, or pocket placements leads to incorrect construction methods. Vague trim descriptions like "silver button" instead of "20mm silver shank button, style SB-201, 2-hole attachment" cause suppliers to source the wrong components. No size chart grading across the full range means manufacturers must guess intermediate sizes, leading to inconsistent fit. Missing label position and size specs results in labels placed incorrectly or at wrong sizes, requiring rework.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Common Tech Pack Mistakes and Solutions</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
        This table lists the eight most common tech pack mistakes, what happens when they occur, and how to fix them. Use this as a checklist when creating or reviewing your tech pack.
      </p>

      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Mistake</th>
              <th>What Happens</th>
              <th>How to Fix</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Missing measurements</strong></td>
              <td>Factory guesses = wrong fit</td>
              <td>Include complete POMs for all sizes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Pantone numbers not specified</strong></td>
              <td>Colours get matched wrong</td>
              <td>Use Pantone TPX for all colours</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Fabric weight not stated</strong></td>
              <td>Wrong hand feel and drape</td>
              <td>Specify GSM for all fabrics</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>No seam allowance noted</strong></td>
              <td>Manufacturer adds differently</td>
              <td>Specify seam allowance (typically 1cm)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Missing construction notes</strong></td>
              <td>Complex areas constructed incorrectly</td>
              <td>Detail special construction techniques</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Vague trim descriptions</strong></td>
              <td>Wrong components sourced</td>
              <td>Specify part numbers and attachment methods</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>No size chart grading</strong></td>
              <td>Inconsistent fit across range</td>
              <td>Include grade rules for all sizes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Missing label position specs</strong></td>
              <td>Labels placed incorrectly</td>
              <td>Document label placement and size</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <caption>Table: Eight common tech pack mistakes with consequences and solutions. Complete tech packs avoid these issues.</caption>
      </div>

      <p class="section__text" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        SDF Clothing reviews all tech packs before production begins and flags any unclear specifications. Our team identifies missing information and requests clarification before sampling starts, preventing costly revisions downstream. For brands who need help creating complete tech packs, our <a href="/tech-pack-service">tech pack service</a> ensures all critical specifications are included. Our <a href="/sampling-service">sampling service</a> includes tech pack review as part of the sample development process.
