  <!-- Section 7: Tech Pack Requirements by Product Type -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <h2 class="section__title">Tech Pack Requirements by Product Type</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Different products require different tech pack depth and complexity. Simple products like basic t-shirts need 4-6 pages of documentation covering essential specifications. Complex products like bomber jackets with multiple components require 12-20 pages of documentation to specify all details accurately. Understanding the tech pack requirements for your product type helps you budget for development time and ensure you include all necessary information.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Simple products like basic t-shirts, polo shirts, and leggings require minimal tech pack documentation because they have few components and straightforward construction. Tech packs for these products typically include front and back flat sketches, a basic measurement spec, fabric composition and weight, color specifications, and basic trim details. Complex products like jackets, coats, and structured dresses require extensive documentation because they have multiple components (linings, interlinings, zippers, buttons, pockets, collars, cuffs), complex construction techniques, and specialized trims.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Activewear sets require additional specifications for performance fabrics, compression ratios, and stretch recovery. Woven shirts need collar and cuff construction details, button placket specifications, and interfacing requirements. Swimwear requires fabric stretch specifications, lining details, and chlorine resistance notes. Outerwear coats require interlining specifications, thermal insulation requirements, and weatherproofing details. The more complex the product, the more detailed the tech pack must be to ensure accurate production.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section__subtitle">Tech Pack Complexity by Product Type</h3>
      <p class="section__text">
